condition_name: Prostatitis
condition_slug: prostatitis
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: "An inflammation of the prostate or pain in the prostate, similar to that caused by an inflammation. Classified into: ・ Acute bacterial prostatitis ・ Chronic bacterial prostatitis ・ Chronic non-bacterial prostatitis ・ Prostatodynia Risk factors: ・ Ductile reflux ・ Urinary tract infection ・ Indwelling urethral catheterization ・ Penetrating anal sex ・ Sexually transmitted infections"
clinical_features[2]:
  - type: Acute prostatitis
    features[9]: Fever,Chills,Malaise,Nausea,Dysuria,Frequency,Haematuria,Urethral discharge,"Hot, boggy, swollen and very tender prostate"
  - type: Chronic prostatitis
    features[11]: Dysuria,Frequency,Urgency,Haematuria,Poor stream,Urethral discharge,Low back pain,Perineal pain,Haemospermia,Painful ejaculation,"Enlarged, tender, firm prostate"
investigations[7]: FBC and ESR,Urinalysis,"Urine microscopy, culture and sensitivity","Prostatic massage: microscopy, culture and sensitivity (chronic prostatitis only)",Trans-rectal ultrasound,"Biopsy: culture and histology",Urethrocystoscopy (chronic prostatitis only)
treatment:
  goals[2]: To eradicate causative organisms,Control pain
  non_drug[3]: Prostatic massage (chronic prostatitis only),Physiotherapy,Sitz baths
  drug[6]: Ciprofloxacin 500 mg orally every 12 hours for 28 days,Cotrimoxazole 960 mg orally every 12 hours for 28 days,"Non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (e.g. diclofenac, ibuprofen)","Steroids (e.g. prednisolone, dexamethasone)",Alpha blockers (e.g. prazosin),Hormonal therapy (e.g. finasteride)
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[0]:
  supportive_measures[0]:
differential_diagnoses[4]: Benign prostatic hypertrophy,Cystitis,Urethral stricture,Prostate cancer
complications[4]: Prostatic abscess,Prostatic calculi,Infertility,Septicaemia
prevention[0]:
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null